## v1.1.2-alpha1

### Upgrade Notes

- Before upgrading, move custom member environment variables from direct DaemonSet edits into `localStorage.member.extraEnv`, or the Cluster's `hwameistor.io/local-storage-member-extra-env` annotation as a JSON environment-variable array; preserve required container binary paths when extending `PATH`.
- To adopt the companion migration behavior, deploy a Local Storage image containing the companion implementation through `localStorage.member.tag` alongside the updated Operator and published migration image; the chart's member default remains `v1.1.1`.
- When adopting the bundled migration image from an older configuration, set `localStorage.migrate.juicesync.tag` to `v1.2.0`, or update `spec.localStorage.member.juicesyncImage.tag` for non-Helm installations; existing nonempty image settings are preserved.
- To retain disabled migration checks, set `localStorage.migrate.check=false`, or `MIGRATE_CHECK=false` on the Operator Deployment for non-Helm installations.
- Wait for the Local Storage rollout before creating migration Jobs with the new settings; existing Jobs and their retry Pods retain their original templates.

### Breaking Changes

- Local Storage environment overrides can now accommodate nonstandard host-tool paths, but direct DaemonSet environment edits are no longer preserved. Manage overrides through `localStorage.member.extraEnv` for new and existing members, including updates and removals. Reconciliation replaces the member environment; malformed Cluster annotation JSON blocks reconciliation. Extending `PATH` does not establish general NixOS compatibility. ([#399](https://github.com/hwameistor/hwameistor-operator/pull/399))

### Changes

- For migrations affected by directory-symlink SFTP failures, the Operator now supports adopting the companion JuiceFS migration implementation and requests content checks by default. With the updated Local Storage controller and migration image, `localStorage.migrate.juicesync.version` selects an installed binary, defaulting to JuiceFS `1.2.0` in image `v1.2.0`. Checks change from disabled to enabled on new and existing members; the companion image uses `--check-all`. Missing binaries fail without fallback. Opt-in `1.4.1` skips special files that `1.2.0` fails to copy, and checks cannot detect those omissions. Neither version provides complete rootfs fidelity or a consistent snapshot of active writes. ARM64 execution and the complete updated-controller PVC migration lifecycle remain unverified. ([#400](https://github.com/hwameistor/hwameistor-operator/pull/400)) **Needs review.**

